/bin/
/plugin/
# The cover twin of /plugin/, and root-owned for the same reason:
# `sudo make create-cover` writes it (the coverage lane, and
# `make capture-fixtures` — #644). Missing here while present in
# .gitignore, it broke every unprivileged `docker build` from the
# repo root on any tree that had built the instrumented plugin.
/plugin-cover/
/multiarch/
# Integration-suite output (#378). The suite targets are root-only, so
# logs/ is created root-owned — the same context-walk hazard as the
# plugin build directories above.
/logs/
# mkdocs-material build output (#133). Never part of the image, and
# large enough that shipping it is pure context bloat.
/site/
.git/
# Nothing in the image needs .claude/, and it is where per-instance git
# worktrees live. A worktree that ever ran `sudo make create` leaves a
# root-owned plugin/rootfs/ behind; once that directory is in the build
# context, every unprivileged `docker build` from the repo root dies in
# the context walk. scripts/check-build-context.sh gates this.
.claude/
.github/
docs/
scripts/
*.md
LICENSE.md
test_env.sh
code-review-report.md
# Credential-shaped paths, mirroring the block .gitignore carries for the
# same reason. Nothing in the image is built from them — the Dockerfile
# copies go.*, cmd/ and pkg/ and nothing else — but `docker build` uploads
# the WHOLE context to the daemon before any COPY is considered, so a
# local secrets/ or .env is transferred even though no instruction names
# it. That is how a developer's SSH private key in ./secrets/ rode along
# on every build from the repo root.
#
# The `**/` prefix is deliberate rather than decorative: a bare `secrets`
# excludes the context root only, while .gitignore's `secrets/` applies at
# any depth. Written this way the two files mean the same thing.
# scripts/check-dockerignore-parity.sh holds them in step.
**/secrets
**/credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.netrc
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
# Editor and interpreter droppings. Ignored by git, never part of a build,
# and __pycache__ is written by scripts/badge-sync.py wherever it runs.
**/.vscode
**/__pycache__
